                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="17366744" author="cnoelle_bfi" created="Mon, 21 Jun 2021 17:18:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Another way to workaround this is to go to /#/interpreter (in the frontend) and edit the mongodb interpretor settings by adding a dependency &quot;org.apache.commons:commons-lang3:3.12.0&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The likely solution to this issue is then to add a dependency on commons-lang3 in the pom.xml of the mongodb interpretor:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/master/mongodb/pom.xml&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/master/mongodb/pom.xml&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Currently, it only declares a dependency on commons-io, although the MongoDbInterpretor also imports org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils, see&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/master/mongodb/src/main/java/org/apache/zeppelin/mongodb/MongoDbInterpreter.java&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/master/mongodb/src/main/java/org/apache/zeppelin/mongodb/MongoDbInterpreter.java&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17369303" author="reamer" created="Fri, 25 Jun 2021 07:30:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Closed with &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/4151&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/4151&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
